    n: 393, slug: 'vacuity-guard',
    plan: `Issue #393 'W3.4 Vacuity guard'. Read the issue and ADR-0009 (D2 and Consequences: additive PropertyOutcome values). Triage found: properties/harness.py::render_semantic_harness emits only __ESBMC_assert((post), "forseti:semantic") after the call; orchestrator/check.py::_outcome_for maps Verified -> HELD unconditionally; PropertyOutcome has held/violated/unknown/error/skipped; precond/reachability.py::classify_site_probe (REACHED/UNREACHABLE/INCONCLUSIVE, needs a non-empty label) and precond/synth.py (NON_VACUITY_LABEL='forseti:non-vacuity', the one probe emitter) are reusable. Build: (1) a probe render mode in properties/harness.py: same body and same k, with a labelled __ESBMC_assert(0, label) after the call and the real assertion omitted; share the label constant / emit helper with precond/synth.py if it is small and behaviour-identical. (2) In check_properties, after a VERIFIED (HELD) verdict at its settled k, run the probe at the same k: REACHED -> HELD, UNREACHABLE -> new PropertyOutcome.VACUOUS, INCONCLUSIVE -> UNKNOWN. Never probe VIOLATED/UNKNOWN/ERROR. (3) Add PropertyOutcome.VACUOUS additively, and handle every consumer: PropertyCheckRun._outcome_for_counts (a vacuous result must never produce run-outcome 'held'; pick and document precedence), to_dict, adapters/claude_code/property_gate.py (vacuous never counts toward acceptance and must be surfaced, not silently dropped), core/check.py, core/cli.py (exit-code mapping and docstrings enumerating outcomes), core/mcp_server.py (payload/docs), core/loop.py if it reads outcomes. (4) Output states the limitation: the probe shows some path reaches the post-call point; it does not show that k covers every path (paths cut by --no-unwinding-assertions can still hide a violation). (5) Tests: fake-port unit tests; ESBMC-gated (skip without esbmc): domain 'x > 0 && x < 0' -> vacuous not HELD; a unit whose loop needs more than k iterations on every input -> vacuous at that k; existing HELD results on examples/ stay HELD (or explain); gate test that vacuous never counts toward acceptance. Do not change the unwind/k policy or any threshold. If a vacuous-vs-run-outcome naming choice is a real design call, take the additive minimal option, document it in the PR, and put the question in needsRuling rather than stalling.`,
  },
